  "notes": "Verified 2026-09-17 by fetching the real archived 2023-24 bulletin page directly (bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2023-2024/.../communication-sciences-disorders-bs/). The Program Requirements course list is byte-identical to CSD-2026.json's (all 29 codes, same pools). The University Park Suggested Academic Plan's course sequence and Gen Ed slot count/position already match 2024-26 exactly (Integrative Studies in Semester 1 and Semester 3 -- printed generically as 'General Education Course (Integrative Studies)' without the later editions' explicit 'Inter-Domain' qualifier, but occupying the identical two slots -- plus Exploration and GA in Semester 4, and the same ASHA-driven GN Human Biological / Physical Science split), so those slots are kept unchanged from CSD-2026.json (tagged gen_ed: INTER-D to match the slot's real later-confirmed identity). PSYCH 100 has no '100H' alternative in this edition's table either, so that option is omitted (same as CSD-2024/2025). One real, structural difference found: the 2023-24 First Year table lists First-Year Seminar as TWO separate 1-credit line items -- 'CSD 297 (First-Year Seminar)' and 'PSU 14' -- totaling 2 credits (Semester 1 total 17, not 16), rather than the single consolidated 'First Year Seminar (1-2 credits)' line that first appears starting in the 2024-25 edition (see CSD-2024.json's notes). Both CSD 297 ('Special Topics', 1 credit) and PSU 14 ('First-Year Seminar Health and Human Development', 1 credit) are real, cataloged courses (Backend/catalogs/csd_catalog.json, Backend/catalogs/psu_catalog.json), so this file models them as two explicit required 1-credit course items rather than one generic slot, and Semester 1's target_credits is bumped to 17 to match. The GWS course-selection (CAS 100A, CAS 100B, CAS 100C, or ENGL/CAS 138T recommended) line matches 2024-2026 exactly; unlike 2022's edition (see CSD-2022.json's notes), the 2023-24 text does not list a bare 'CAS 100' option. Total credit range printed on the page is 120 (a single number, not a range, unlike every other year's 120-124/121-126).",
